"""
Write the reference of the setup script: for every item, the exact commands that ticking it runs and that unticking
it runs to put things back, with a diff for every file they edit and a link to the code behind them.

    .github/scripts/generate-setup-reference.py          # rewrite the pages
    .github/scripts/generate-setup-reference.py --check  # fail when they no longer match the script

What the items run is not written down here. The script is imported and every item's own builders are run, the same
functions the window runs, on a machine that is described instead of read: a fresh CachyOS install for turning things
on, and the same machine with everything set up for turning things off. So the pages cannot say anything the window
does not do, and a change to the script that is not reflected in them fails the quality checks.

The files the setup script edits are fed the files a fresh Arch install ships (see STOCK below), so the diffs on the
site are what happens on a stock machine. The window shows the diff against your own files before it applies one.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

